==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From Early Modern English {{m|en|conferre}}, from {{uder|en|frm|conférer}}, from {{uder|en|fro|conferer}}, from {{uder|en|la|cōnferō}}. Compare {{cog|nl|confereren}}, {{cog|de|konferieren}}, {{cog|da|konferere}}, {{cog|sv|konferera}}. {{doublet|en|collate}}. See also [[infer]], [[relate]] and [[refer]], [[delate]] and [[defer]], as well as [[prelate]] and [[prefer]] among others.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɜː/|a=RP,AU}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-confer.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɜɹ/|[kʰə̥ɱˈfɝ]|a=GenAm,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-confer.wav|a=North Carolina}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈføː/|a=NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɛr/|a=Scotland}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfeː/|a=Scouse,square-nurse}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɛː/|a=Humberside,Teesside,square-nurse}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɜː(ɹ)/|a=Lancashire,square-nurse}}
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈfɜ(ɾ)/|a=Indic}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[grant]] as a possession; to [[bestow]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|afford}}
#: {{ux|en|The college has '''conferred''' an honorary degree upon the visiting Prime Minister.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1671|author=w:John Milton|title=w:Samson Agonistes
|passage=Nor shall I count in hainous to enjoy<br>The public marks of honour and reward<br> '''Conferr'd''' upon me{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Andrew Rawnsley|journal=The Observer|date=7 Feb 2010
|passage=The special immunities that are '''conferred''' on MPs were framed with the essential purpose of allowing them to speak freely in parliament.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To talk together, to [[consult]], [[discuss]]; to [[collogue]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|palaver}}
#: {{ux|en|They were in a huddle, '''conferring''' about something.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|title=A Traveler's Perils|date=25 Mar 1974
|passage=Local buttons popped when Henry Kissinger visited Little Rock last month to '''confer''' with Fulbright on the Middle East oil talks.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[compare]]. {{defdate|16th–18th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|part=II|section=3|member=1|subsection=i|passage='''Confer''' thine estate with others&nbsp;[&hellip;]. Be content and rest satisfied, for thou art well in respect to others&nbsp;[&hellip;].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1661|author=w:Robert Boyle|title=The Second Essay, of Unsucceeding Experiments
|passage=If we '''confer''' these observations with others of the like nature, we may find cause to rectify the general opinion.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To bring together; to [[collect]], [[gather]]. {{defdate|16th–17th c.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To contribute; to [[conduce]]. {{defdate|16th–18th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Glanvill Scepsis Scientifica|passage=The closeness and compactness of the parts resting together doth much '''confer''' to the strength of the union.}}

